# kuuki-pod firmware project parameters (ticket 14b).
#
# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# The Pod's product decisions — how often a Measurement is promoted to a Sample,
# and how far back the Buffer keeps Samples — live here, on the configuration
# surface, not inside the modules that happen to use them. The ring Buffer is
# handed a plain capacity derived from these (see src/app_config.h) and knows
# nothing about either.

menu "kuuki-pod"

config KUUKI_SAMPLE_INTERVAL_SEC
	int "Sample tick interval, seconds"
	default 900
	range 1 86400
	help
	  The Sample tick cadence: the Pod promotes one of the SCD40's
	  Measurements to a Sample this often. 900 (15 minutes) is the v1
	  cadence the webapp's Merge snaps slots to (CONTEXT.md), so changing it
	  changes what a slot means on the wire. The Buffer is resized to still
	  span KUUKI_RETENTION_SEC, which this must divide evenly — a build with
	  a leftover fails on a BUILD_ASSERT rather than quietly spanning less.

config KUUKI_RETENTION_SEC
	int "Buffer retention target, seconds"
	default 2592000
	range 1 31536000
	help
	  How far back the in-RAM Buffer keeps Samples before overwriting its
	  oldest. 2592000 (30 days) is the v1 target. Must be a whole number of
	  Sample intervals; the resulting ring costs 12 bytes of RAM per Sample,
	  paid once — a Sync streams straight out of the ring, with no second
	  copy of it.

endmenu

source "Kconfig.zephyr"
